.TH QCOM-ATH-BOARD-UPDATE 8 "September 2026" "qcom-ath-board-update" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
qcom-ath-board-update \- install Qualcomm ath11k/ath12k board data from Windows
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qcom-ath-board-update
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ inspect | install | verify ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B qcom-ath-board-update
detects a Qualcomm PCI Wi-Fi device, obtains its complete Linux board
identifier from the kernel log, and reads the Windows
.B BDFilename
registry value from the active SYSTEM control set. It then uses Qualcomm's
bdencoder utility to add the selected BDF to the appropriate
.B board-2.bin
container.
.PP
The default command is
.BR inspect ,
which makes no firmware changes. The
.B install
command writes an overlay below
.B /usr/lib/firmware/updates
and optionally rebuilds the initramfs. The
.B verify
command fails unless the selected BDF is already mapped to the target board
identifier.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --device " PCI_ADDRESS"
Select a PCI device when more than one candidate exists.
.TP
.BI --windows-root " PATH"
Use an already mounted Windows system volume.
.TP
.BI --windows-device " DEVICE"
Use a specific NTFS or BitLocker block device.
.TP
.BI --bdf-file " PATH"
Use a board ELF directly instead of reading the Windows registry.
.TP
.BI --board-container " PATH"
Override the source board-2.bin or board-2.bin.zst.
.TP
.BI --board-name " IDENTIFIER"
Override the complete board identifier.
.TP
.BI --firmware-relative-path " PATH"
Override the firmware path relative to /usr/lib/firmware.
.TP
.BI --output-root " PATH"
Override the firmware overlay root. The default is
.BR /usr/lib/firmware/updates .
.TP
.B --no-initramfs-update
Do not run update-initramfs or dracut after installation.
.TP
.B --json
Print the inspection report as JSON.
.TP
.B -v ", " --verbose
Print diagnostic detail (discovered devices, kernel-log matches, board
container search paths, and Windows registry lookups) to standard error.
Repeat for more detail
.RB ( -vv " prints a full Python traceback for unexpected errors)."
.SH BITLOCKER
BitLocker volumes are opened with dislocker in read-only mode. Dislocker
prompts for a recovery password without exposing it in the process command
line. TPM-only protectors generally require the volume to be unlocked in
Windows first.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /usr/lib/firmware/updates/ath11k
ath11k firmware overlays.
.TP
.B /usr/lib/firmware/updates/ath12k
ath12k firmware overlays.
.TP
.B /var/lib/qcom-ath-board-update/manifest.json
Manifest describing the most recent installation.
.TP
.B /var/lib/qcom-ath-board-update/backups
Previous overlay files replaced by the tool.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns zero on success and non-zero on detection, validation, registry,
encoder, installation, or verification errors.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mount-windows (8),
.BR umount-windows (8),
.BR dislocker-fuse (1),
.BR update-initramfs (8),
.BR dracut (8)
